1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:03,960
Airplane windows used to be square, and the planes ripped apart in the sky.

2
00:00:04,620 --> 00:00:07,759
Why? every flight, the cabin is pumped up like a balloon.

3
00:00:08,259 --> 00:00:11,759
At a sharp corner, all that push piles up in one tiny spot.

4
00:00:12,199 --> 00:00:14,539
Flight after flight, a crack grows right there.

5
00:00:14,900 --> 00:00:18,905
In 1954, two of the first jetliners broke apart in mid-air.

6
00:00:19,269 --> 00:00:23,000
Engineers sank one in a water tank and pumped it up, again and again.

7
00:00:23,400 --> 00:00:26,739
After about 3,000 flights, it split open at a window corner.

8
00:00:27,108 --> 00:00:30,359
A round corner spreads the push all the way around. no weak spot.

9
00:00:30,820 --> 00:00:32,984
So next time you fly, remember:
